  "title": "Ionization, melting-point and measured-logP INPUTS",
  "description": "Acid/base dissociation constants, melting points and measured octanol-water partition coefficients, per compound id, taken from the compendial and primary physicochemical literature.",
  "note": "EVERY NUMBER IN THIS FILE IS AN INPUT, NOT A PREDICTION. BioCAD contains no pKa predictor and no melting-point predictor, and it never guesses either one. A compound absent from this pack therefore yields Provenance::NotComputed on every pKa-dependent or melting-point-dependent quantity, naming the missing input - it does not fall back to an assumed default. A group list that is present but empty is itself a cited statement: it means the source reports no dissociation in the 0-14 range, which is different from the compound being absent. Values are the aqueous 25 C thermodynamic or apparent constants as reported; where a source gives a range the reported centre is used and the range is not narrowed. Sources are described in prose because a described source can be checked; a fabricated DOI or page number cannot.",
  "sources": {
    "crc": "CRC Handbook of Chemistry and Physics, the 'Dissociation Constants of Organic Acids and Bases' and 'Physical Constants of Organic Compounds' tables",
